codex
The two pages are independent: Alpha uses 8 KiB pages, and `0x6000` and `0x4000` occupy cache slots 3 and 2. Invalidating slot 3 leaves slot 2 populated, even though they share the same cache table.

I also confirmed that selectors 1, 2, and 3 all make the same invalidation call. The new rows can pin the predicate bounds and cache scope; their comments should not claim separate ITB and DTB behavior.
